(;B[so]C[Seki - but if he had played one point lower White would be unconditionally
dead. (After that Black could fill all the outside liberties
and then make an"eye in the belly" by playing one point above
211. If at any stage White tried to prevent this, White could
reduce the stones inside to a one eyed lump.) 
]
